@anionex/dsh-smarter-edit README · 3. Structured JSON overhead：The model must also encode multiline source inside a schema:

```json
{
  "old_string": "...",
  "new_string": "..."
}

Quoting, escaping, and the exact-match fields belong to the editor protocol,
not the code change. Freeform `apply_patch` lets the model generate the editing
language itself.

@anionex/dsh-smarter-edit README · Additional capabilities：Besides changing the editing tool exposed to the model, Smarter Edit supports:

- multiple ordered hunks;
- add, update, move, and delete operations;
- Codex-compatible contextual matching;
- failure-atomic preflight and rollback;
- native DSH diff rendering.

@anionex/dsh-smarter-edit README · How it works：The plugin removes model-visible `edit`, `write`, and legacy
`str_replace_editor` plus their prompt sections while replacement mode is
active. Unloading it restores the original tools.

@anionex/dsh-smarter-edit README · Implementation details：See [Implementation Notes](docs/implementation.md) for Codex alignment,
failure atomicity, line-ending behavior, package entry points, and provider
transport.
